{title: Elishama Son of Ammihud}
{subtitle: Numbers 1:10; 2:18; 7:48–53; 10:22; 1 Chronicles 7:26–27}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 87}
{time: 6/8}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] |
| [Bb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Bb] |
| [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
From the sons of Joseph came a line
[Eb]Ephraim stood with heart and mind
[Bb]Ammihud named, his fa[Gm]ther was
Elisha[F]ma led the chosen class
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Elis[Bb]hama son of Ammihud
[Eb]Leader of the tribe that stood
On the [Bb]west side under [Gm]flag
Guiding [F]Israel through the [Bb]track
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
When the camp was set in order
[Eb]Standard raised to find the border
E[Bb]lishama led the [Gm]people through
[F]With the census count to [Bb]view
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Elishama son of Ammihud
[Eb]Leader of the tribe that stood
On the [Bb]west side under [Gm]flag
Guiding [F]Israel through the [Bb]track
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Seventh day his offering came
[Eb]Silver plate and basin frame
[Bb]Fine flour mixed with [Gm]oil so sweet
[F]Gold dish filled, the al[Bb]tar kept
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Nun his [Gm]son, then [Eb]Joshua [Bb]came
Lineage recor[Gm]ded, ne[F]ver the [Bb]same
{end_of_verse}
